WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.351
Start your explanation with the main point in one sentence.

00:00:03.351 --> 00:00:06.190
For example, please submit the document by Friday.

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:10.393
Tell your listener what they need to do before you explain the background.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.542
Use this order: point, reason, example.

00:00:22.542 --> 00:00:24.498
The document is due on Friday.

00:00:24.498 --> 00:00:26.584
We need it for Monday's meeting.

00:00:26.584 --> 00:00:30.756
For example, save it to the shared folder by three pm on Friday.

00:00:30.756 --> 00:00:32.972
Connect the action to its purpose.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.197
At the end, ask the listener to describe their next action.

00:00:43.197 --> 00:00:45.743
For example, when and where will you submit it?

00:00:45.743 --> 00:00:50.945
Hearing the answer in their own words can reveal misunderstandings that a simple yes would miss.
